{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChJpVbakQRJ3HXDTvrQeS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`ccode(sinc(x))` now prints the Piecewise form the issue suggested:\n\n```\n((Ne(x, 0)) ? (\n   sin(x)/x\n)\n: (\n   1\n))\n```\n\nThe existing `sympy/printing/tests/test_ccode.py` passes (30 tests).\n\nThe cause was that the C printer had no handler for `sinc`, so it fell through to the \"Not supported in C\" fallback. I added a `_print_sinc` method in `sympy/printing/ccode.py` that builds `Piecewise((sin(x)/x, Ne(x, 0)), (1, True))` and prints that.\n\nI didn't add a test for `sinc`, since I wasn't to edit test files. Also, `Ne(x, 0)` is printed literally, exactly as in the issue's example output, so the generated string isn't compilable C as written."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":936,"cache_read_input_tokens":19909,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":936},"output_tokens":280,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e27e9bcb-9f2d-4ab7-816e-78a7e3debefa","uuid":"4167d936-5ca4-4305-be9c-30113585a6f1","timestamp":"2026-11-22T23:17:17.326Z","request_id":"req_011ChJpVbSp1gf6uGpwyqSxv"}
